package testdata

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Opus Deep Dive 2026-05-05 (batch 2) — four LOLBIN edge-case rules covering
// debugger / packet-capture / pager / editor classes:
//
//   1. gdb -ex 'shell|pi|python|pipe' direct shell-escape ex commands.
//      Sister rule ts-block-gdb-batch-exec covers `call (int)system(...)`
//      only; the `shell`, `pi` (python-interactive), `python`, and `pipe`
//      ex-commands need no attached process and were uncovered.
//   2. tcpdump -z postrotate-command — runs CMD on every rotated capture.
//      Real LOLBIN; legit compression values (gzip, bzip2, xz, zstd, lz4,
//      compress) are explicitly NOT matched.
//   3. man -P / --pager= override — pager replaced with a shell, language
//      interpreter, or /tmp script. Sister to MANPAGER= env-var hijack.
//   4. emacs --batch --eval '(shell-command ...)' — Lisp shell-spawn.
//      Editor-as-LOLBIN peer of ts-block-vim-shell-escape-cli.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

